implementationPlan.description:
Edit packages/moe-daemon/README.md with the Edit tool only. This is a docs-only row: no code, no new test file, and no test suite to run. The architect's dry-run copy of the result is /mnt/d/moe-scratch/plan-52d7/README.proposed.md.

In "### Start Daemon" Options (:35-37):
- replace `- \`--project, -p\` - Project path (required)` with `- \`--project\` - Project path. Defaults to \`MOE_PROJECT_PATH\`, then the current directory.` (parseArgs, index.ts:62 and :67: --project, else MOE_PROJECT_PATH, else process.cwd());
- keep the `--port` line;
- add `- \`--host\` - Bind address. Defaults to \`MOE_BIND_HOST\`, then \`127.0.0.1\`; \`--host\` wins over \`MOE_BIND_HOST\`. \`wsl\` binds loopback plus the WSL adapters. A value other than \`127.0.0.1\` is recorded as \`bindHost\` in \`.moe/daemon.json\` (see \`docs/CONFIGURATION.md\`).` (index.ts:65 and :70; the daemon.json write at :876; CONFIGURATION.md:16 and :30);
- after the list, add a blank line and `\`init\` takes the same options.` parseArgs is shared, and init passes port and host to superviseDaemon.

In "### Logging" (:80), replace the `MOE_LOG_LEVEL` line with `- \`LOG_LEVEL\` - Log level (\`debug\`, \`info\`, \`warn\`, \`error\`). Default: \`info\`` (util/logger.ts:7 reads `process.env.LOG_LEVEL || 'info'`).

Change nothing else. Do not add a `-p` alias, and do not rename the env var in code: task-88673297 holds index.ts, and a rename would break LOG_LEVEL users. Line 71's daemon.json comment is stale too (`{ port, pid, startedAt }`), but it is out of this row's scope; leave it.

Verification (once, fresh, from the task worktree root). Run executionContract.checkRefs [0] and then [1], joined with ' && '. Submit that exact text, its exit code and the output tail as complete_task's verification.

[0] is DoD 1 to DoD 3's mechanical check. It prints DOC_OK only when all of these hold:
- `grep -nE -- '(^|[^-])-p\b|MOE_LOG_LEVEL|\(required\)'` finds nothing in the README;
- the LOG_LEVEL line carries `Default: \`info\``;
- the --project line names MOE_PROJECT_PATH and the current directory;
- every `--flag` in the README is an `indexOf('--flag')` in packages/moe-daemon/src/index.ts;
- every flag index.ts parses appears in the README.

[1] is the scope check: only packages/moe-daemon/README.md may differ, plus .moe/.

Error handling for a red check:
- [0] prints the offending README line, or the flag that is unparsed or missing. Fix the README text, never the check.
- [1] names the stray path. Revert it.

The architect's dry run printed DOC_OK on the proposed text. The base README failed [0], and two mutants failed it too: an unparsed `--frobnicate` and a missing `--host`.
